Origin:
Firmware commands shared one queue with data frames and waited behind
them; with the transmit window closed they timed out unsent. Commands now
have their own queue and go first, a command that waited a second is sent
once past the window, and a window the firmware got wrong is replaced by
two frames as in Linux. A sequence number is spent only on a successful
write. bwfm_proto_bcdc_set_dcmd no longer leaks its buffer on a firmware
error. The Raspberry Pi 5 run passed with and without this change.
